# Line endings are a CORRECTNESS constraint in this repository, not a style
# preference, so they are pinned rather than left to the machine's git config.
#
# Why: `lib/client.js` is assembled by concatenating `src/client/index.js`
# VERBATIM with the shell in `src/client/.shell.json`, and `verify-bundle.mjs`
# asserts the result is byte-identical to the deployed artifact. The shell's
# prelude/epilogue strings in that JSON contain real newlines, and the client
# body contains CSS string literals. Under `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on
# this machine — a fresh checkout would rewrite every LF as CRLF, changing the
# assembled bytes and breaking the very equality the gate exists to protect.
# (It would fail loudly rather than silently, but a gate that fires on every
# clone is a gate people learn to ignore.)
#
# `eol=lf` fixes the working tree to LF on every platform, which is also what
# the upstream project is authored in.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary or generated content that must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
pnpm-lock.yaml -text
